  "result": "Done! I've added foreign currency support to `src/money.js` with currency conversion and formatting functions.\n\n**Implementation:**\n\n**RATES constant:**\n```javascript\n{ EUR: 1, USD: 1.085, GBP: 0.8425 }\n```\n\n**`convert(cents, currency)` function:**\n- Takes EUR cents and target currency code\n- Returns `ok(amountInTargetCurrency)` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n- Uses banker's rounding to whole cents\n- Example: `convert(10000, 'USD')` \u2192 `ok(10850)` (\u20ac100 = $108.50)\n\n**`formatMoney(cents, currency)` function:**\n- Takes EUR cents and target currency code\n- Returns formatted string with appropriate symbol or error\n- Formats with 2 decimals and currency symbol: `$100.50`, `\u20ac100.00`, `\u00a384.25`\n- Example: `formatMoney(10000, 'USD')` \u2192 `ok('$108.50')`\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- Returns `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')` for unrecognized currencies (EUR, USD, GBP only)\n- Added UNKNOWN_CURRENCY error code to `src/errors.js`\n\n**Test Coverage (30 tests):**\n- RATES values and keys\n- Currency validation\n- EUR-to-USD conversion (\u00d71.085)\n- EUR-to-GBP conversion (\u00d70.8425)\n- EUR-to-EUR pass-through (unchanged)\n- Proper rounding (banker's rounding to whole cents)\n- Formatting with correct symbols (\u20ac, $, \u00a3)\n- Consistent 2-decimal format\n- Edge cases: zero, negative, large amounts, small amounts (1 cent)\n- Consistency across multiple calls\n\n**All 311 tests pass** (30 new currency + 281 existing).",
